{"page":614,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.05257,"w":0.33117,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"600 Chapter 10: Infinite Sequences and Series"},{"x":0.04849,"y":0.09093,"w":0.25603,"h":0.03581,"fs":0.03581,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"10.4 Comparison Tests"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.13687,"w":0.593,"h":0.0435,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"We have seen how to determine the convergence of geometric series, p-series, and a few others. We can test the convergence of many more series by comparing their terms to those of a series whose convergence is known."},{"x":0.35358,"y":0.21056,"w":0.53247,"h":0.02882,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"THEOREM 10—The Comparison Test Let gan, gcn, and gdn be series with nonnegative terms. Suppose that for some integer N"},{"x":0.49609,"y":0.24893,"w":0.2434,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"dn … an … cn for all n 7 N."},{"x":0.35358,"y":0.27195,"w":0.31807,"h":0.03416,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"(a) If gcn converges, then gan also converges. (b) If gdn diverges, then gan also diverges."},{"x":0.07323,"y":0.27415,"w":0.01071,"h":0.01216,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"c1"},{"x":0.09339,"y":0.2944,"w":0.01137,"h":0.01215,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"c2"},{"x":0.11468,"y":0.31221,"w":0.01072,"h":0.01216,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"c3"},{"x":0.13522,"y":0.32818,"w":0.09428,"h":0.02928,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"c4 c5 cn−1 cn"},{"x":0.07286,"y":0.33104,"w":0.0529,"h":0.01827,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"a1 a2 a3"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.3368,"w":0.44896,"h":0.01542,"fs":0.01311,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Proof In Part (a), the partial sums of gan are bounded above by"},{"x":0.13591,"y":0.34809,"w":0.11411,"h":0.02846,"fs":0.01023,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"a4 a5 an ···"},{"x":0.08533,"y":0.35842,"w":0.19102,"h":0.01812,"fs":0.01023,"n":7,"k":0,"t":"n 1 2 3 4 5 n−1 n"},{"x":0.49557,"y":0.37561,"w":0.21824,"h":0.01695,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"M = a1 + a2 + g+ aN + a"},{"x":0.72395,"y":0.37627,"w":0.01637,"h":0.01432,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"cn."},{"x":0.68634,"y":0.39039,"w":0.03763,"h":0.00916,"fs":0.0087,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"n=N+1"},{"x":0.04849,"y":0.401,"w":0.23229,"h":0.05968,"fs":0.01151,"n":5,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 10.12 If the total area gcn of the taller cn rectangles is finite, then so is the total area gan of the shorter an rectangles."},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.4063,"w":0.59303,"h":0.04417,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"They therefore form a nondecreasing sequence with a limit L … M. That is, if gcn con- verges, then so does gan. Figure 10.12 depicts this result, where each term of each series is interpreted as the area of a rectangle (just as we did for the Integral Test in Figure 10.11)."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.45234,"w":0.59299,"h":0.03033,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"In Part (b), the partial sums of gan are not bounded from above. If they were, the partial sums for gdn would be bounded by"},{"x":0.49313,"y":0.50158,"w":0.22586,"h":0.02142,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"M* = d1 + d2 + g+ dN + a"},{"x":0.72913,"y":0.50672,"w":0.01365,"h":0.01432,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"an"},{"x":0.69151,"y":0.52084,"w":0.03763,"h":0.00916,"fs":0.0087,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"n=N+1"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.53675,"w":0.34184,"h":0.01498,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"and gdn would have to converge instead of diverge."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.5677,"w":0.38214,"h":0.01449,"fs":0.01407,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 1 We apply Theorem 10 to several series."},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.5924,"w":0.09622,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"(a) The series"},{"x":0.60555,"y":0.61592,"w":0.04886,"h":0.02736,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"5 5n - 1"},{"x":0.58191,"y":0.63722,"w":0.02065,"h":0.00916,"fs":0.0087,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"n=1"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.6538,"w":0.21841,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"diverges because its nth term"},{"x":0.5437,"y":0.67731,"w":0.0979,"h":0.02736,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"5 5n - 1 = 1"},{"x":0.66537,"y":0.67747,"w":0.02651,"h":0.02398,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"7 1 n"},{"x":0.61708,"y":0.69171,"w":0.04078,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"n - 1"},{"x":0.05994,"y":0.72261,"w":0.1615,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"HISTORICAL BIOGRAPHY"},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.72541,"w":0.42331,"h":0.03199,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"is greater than the nth term of the divergent harmonic series. (b) The series"},{"x":0.05994,"y":0.73808,"w":0.09838,"h":0.02365,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Albert of Saxony (ca. 1316–1390)"},{"x":0.52529,"y":0.76827,"w":0.08155,"h":0.02742,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"1 n! = 1 + 1"},{"x":0.59594,"y":0.76828,"w":0.13878,"h":0.02743,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"1! + 1 2! + 1 3! + g"},{"x":0.50165,"y":0.78941,"w":0.02065,"h":0.00916,"fs":0.0087,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"n=0"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.80601,"w":0.59297,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"converges because its terms are all positive and less than or equal to the corresponding"},{"x":0.35277,"y":0.82135,"w":0.05407,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"terms of"},{"x":0.54493,"y":0.84501,"w":0.20272,"h":0.02872,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"1 2n = 1 + 1 + 1 2 + 1 22 + g."},{"x":0.48795,"y":0.85136,"w":0.05233,"h":0.01694,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"1 + a"},{"x":0.52129,"y":0.86614,"w":0.02065,"h":0.00916,"fs":0.0087,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"n=0"},{"x":0.32334,"y":0.88018,"w":0.39066,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The geometric series on the left converges and we have"},{"x":0.55824,"y":0.90384,"w":0.17609,"h":0.02801,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"1 2n = 1 + 1 1 - (1>2) = 3."},{"x":0.50126,"y":0.91019,"w":0.05232,"h":0.01695,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"1 + a"},{"x":0.5346,"y":0.92497,"w":0.02065,"h":0.00916,"fs":0.0087,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"n=0"}]}